  Columns 1-2 read the claimed tokens against the recomputed reference and
  need NO seed. Columns 3-4 are the seeded replay. An honest speculative
  server matches the honest server on 1-2 and not on 3-4 -- which is the
  finding: what the seeded verifier reports is a break in SEED
  SYNCHRONISATION, not in the distribution the tokens were drawn from.

  The mechanism in one number: the verifier's replay reproduces 97.5% of an
  honest sequential server's tokens and only 72.1% of an honest speculative server's --
  against 70.3% for the wrong-seed ATTACK.

